==Campus Life==

=== Food, Utilities & Energy Lounge ===
Startorch Food, Utilities & Energy Lounge (FUEL) is open 24h to all students and staff, providing fully-automatic, intelligent, customisable catering services. Powered by intelligent solutions such as the "Human Energy Assessment and Replenishment System," FUEL offers finely curated menus that balance nutrition and flavour. No matter your dietary options, they make sure every dish on the menu meets both nutritional and personal needs. No more worrying about what to eat - FUEL has you covered.
===Resonator Nursing Unit===
Resonator Nursing Unit (ReNU) is the Academy's infirmary, operating as an affiliate of Rabelle College. It is renowned for its specialisation in Frequency Theraputics. ReNU combines cutting edge medical facilities with frontrunning expertise in treating a wide range of medical conditions. For Startorch students, who undergo intensive training from enrollment through graduation, ReNU offers not only medical support but also a space for stress relief. Resident physician Dr. Luuk Herssen makes sure every student receives close medical attention for their physical and mental wellbeing. The unit members include:

* Dr. Luuk Herssen - Doctor and head of the ReNU
* N.A.N.A. - Nightingale Autonomous Nursing Assistant
* Arman

===Academy Dorm===
The Startorch Academy dorms offer every student their own private space to relax and recharge. Every space in the building is thoughtfully designed to meet a variety of needs. The resting area creates a calming environment that helps even insomniacs rest with ease. Soundproofed walls minimise noise complaints, ensuring peace of mind. Students are also free to rearrange or decorate their rooms as they like - so long as it's within school regulations.
===Auto-Clean Pod===
Auto-Clean Pods are the Academy's intelligent modules that offer highly efficient, fully automated laundromat services that integrate garment cleaning with nano-repair technology. It automatically identifies fabric types and applies tailored care programs, effectively repairing damage and extending garment lifespan. The academy encourages faculty and students to make active use of this facility.
===Uniform Consult & Design===
UNICODE is the Academy's uniform store, where students and staff visit for bespoke uniform tailoring services. The store's intelligent fitting systems ensure each uniform is measured and tailored to the customer. The measurement data is encrypted and accessible only with authorisation, ensuring full protection of customer privacy.
===Recreative Program Generator===
RPGs are modular entertainment units found around the residential quarter of the Academy where the "tenth art" is on full display. According to Rabelle College studies, when combined with Frequency Modulation technologies, video games can help students relieve stress, regulate mood, and restore cognitive wellbeing. The Academy encourages students to balance their academic effort with entertainment to achieve better results.
===Startorch Can & Tin===
The Academy's official convenience store branch that brings grocery shopping right to students and staff's doorstep. From snacks to stationery, the stores carry everything you need for daily life. Every item is handpicked and carefully stocked to ensure consistent quality. "Startorch Can & Tin - bringing you joyful surprises, just like opening a can." It is also where the Gastro-Alchemist Fan Club hangs.
===Auto Parking & Engineering Xpertise===
Auto Parking & Engineering Xpertise (APEX) is a comprehensive space that offers parking and vehicle modification services. Here, students and staff can access not only comprehensive facilities that meet diverse demands but also professional maintenance and vehicle customisation support.
===Auditorium===
The public auditorium in Startorch Academy that serves as the primary venue for large-scale indoor events. It is available for student activities. To host an event here, student societies or fan clubs must submit a proposal and application to the Student Council at least three working days in advance. Upon approval, the event will be officially registered and circulated.

